A federal fishery management program under Section 303A of the Magnuson-Stevens Fishery Conservation and Management Act (MSA) that allocates a specific portion of the total allowable catch of a fishery to individuals, corporations, cooperatives, communities, or regional fishery associations. A LAPP is a type of catch share program; not all catch share programs are LAPPs.  Because a LAPP is a specific legal designation, such a program must meet specific statutory requirements under MSA section 303A to be classified as a LAPP.  MSA section 3(26) defines the term "limited access privilege" as follows: "The term 'limited access privilege' - (A) means a Federal permit, issued as part of a limited access system under [MSA] section 303A to harvest a quantity of fish expressed by a unit or units representing a portion of the total allowable catch of the fishery that may be received or held for exclusive use by a person; and (B) includes an individual fishing quota; but (C) does not include community development quotas as described in [MSA] section 305(i)."
